   "lv": "e",
   "q": "What are the phases of the Software Testing Life Cycle?",
   "hint": "Six phases, starting with understanding the requirements and ending with closure.",
   "answer": "Requirement analysis, test planning, test case design (and test data preparation), test environment setup, test execution (with defect reporting), and test closure.",
   "explain": "<p>Each phase has entry and exit criteria. For example, test execution starts when the build is deployed, smoke testing has passed and test cases are reviewed. Closure produces the test summary report, metrics and lessons learned.</p>"
