   "id": "levels",
   "topic": "Levels and types",
   "lv": "e",
   "q": "What are the levels of testing?",
   "hint": "Start from the smallest piece of code and go up to the customer.",
   "answer": "Unit testing checks individual functions or classes, usually by developers. Integration testing checks that modules work together. System testing checks the complete system against requirements. Acceptance testing checks that the system meets business needs, done by users or clients, and includes alpha and beta testing.",
   "explain": "<p>Integration testing has approaches such as top down (using stubs for missing lower modules), bottom up (using drivers for missing upper modules), sandwich and big bang.</p>"
