   "answer": "Retesting runs the failed test cases again to confirm that a specific defect is fixed. Regression testing runs a wider set of tests to make sure that the fix or new change has not broken existing features that used to work.",
   "explain": "<p>Retesting is planned for specific defects and cannot easily be automated in advance. Regression testing is repeated every release, which makes it the best candidate for automation. Retesting comes first, then regression.</p>"
