   "q": "What are black box, white box and grey box testing?",
   "hint": "How much does the tester know about the internal code?",
   "answer": "Black box testing checks behaviour against requirements without looking at the code. White box testing designs tests from the internal structure, such as statements, branches and paths. Grey box testing combines both, for example a tester who knows the database schema or the API calls behind a screen.",
   "explain": "<p>White box coverage measures include statement coverage, branch (decision) coverage and path coverage. 100 percent branch coverage implies 100 percent statement coverage, but not the reverse.</p>"
