   "answer": "Equivalence partitioning gives three partitions: below 18 (invalid), 18 to 60 (valid) and above 60 (invalid), so one value from each, such as 10, 35 and 70. Boundary value analysis tests the edges: 17, 18, 19 and 59, 60, 61.",
   "explain": "<p>Also think about inputs outside the numeric range: empty, letters, decimals such as 18.5, negative numbers, very large numbers and leading spaces. Two value BVA uses only the boundary and the value just outside (17, 18, 60, 61). Three value BVA adds the value just inside, as above.</p>",
