   "q": "When do you use decision table testing? Build one for a login with a valid or invalid user and password.",
   "hint": "Each condition is true or false, so two conditions give four rules.",
   "answer": "Use a decision table when the output depends on combinations of conditions. With two conditions there are 2² = 4 rules: valid user and valid password goes to the home page, and the other three combinations show an error message.",
   "explain": "<table><tr><th>Rule</th><th>User valid</th><th>Password valid</th><th>Expected</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Home page</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td><td>Error message</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>Error message</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Error message</td></tr></table><p>With n true or false conditions there are 2ⁿ rules. Rules with the same outcome can be collapsed to reduce the number of tests.</p>"
