   "topic": "Test design techniques",
   "lv": "m",
   "q": "What is state transition testing? Give an example.",
   "hint": "Think about something that behaves differently depending on what happened before.",
   "answer": "State transition testing models the system as states, events and transitions, and tests valid and invalid transitions. Example: an account locks after three wrong passwords. States are Attempt 1, Attempt 2, Attempt 3 and Locked. A wrong password moves to the next state, a correct one goes to Logged in, and in Locked even the correct password is refused.",
   "explain": "<p>Cover every valid transition at least once, then test invalid ones, such as trying to log in while Locked, or cancelling an order that has already been shipped. ATM sessions, order status flows and traffic lights are popular examples.</p>"
