   "answer": "A tester logs the bug as New. A lead reviews it and sets it to Assigned (or Open) for a developer. The developer fixes it and sets Fixed, then it is sent for retesting. If the fix works the tester sets Closed, and if not, Reopened, which sends it back to the developer.",
   "explain": "<p>Side states: Rejected (not a bug, works as designed), Duplicate (already logged), Deferred or Postponed (to be fixed in a later release), and Cannot Reproduce (the developer could not see it, so add more steps, logs or a video). Exact names vary between tools such as Jira, so mention the workflow your team used.</p>"
