   "topic": "Defect management",
   "lv": "h",
   "q": "What are defect leakage and defect density, and how do you use them?",
   "hint": "Both are ratios.",
   "answer": "Defect leakage is the share of defects found after a testing phase, for example in UAT or production, compared with all defects found. Defect density is the number of defects per size of the module, such as per thousand lines of code or per function point.",
   "explain": "<span class=\"eq\">Defect leakage = defects found later ÷ (defects found in testing + defects found later) × 100</span><p>If testing found 90 defects and production found 10, the leakage is 10 ÷ 100 × 100 = 10 percent. High leakage points to coverage gaps. High density in one module tells you where to focus regression testing.</p>"
